  "caption": "Quinn sleeps like a chaotic starfish and wakes up with a very opinionated neck. Then the 3am aches feel louder.\n\nThere's no single perfect sleeping position, and moving around at night is normal. During sore phases, small pillow tweaks can take some stress off.\n\nIdeas that often help: a pillow between the knees for a sore back (or under the knees if you're on your back), a pillow that keeps your neck level, sleeping on the other side and hugging a pillow for a sore shoulder, and giving a new setup three to five nights.\n\nNight pain that no position eases, or that comes with fever, weight loss or feeling unwell, needs a check with your GP.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
